{"slug":"ILO__STRIKES","id":"STRIKES","agency":"ILOSTAT","version":"1.0","name":"Strikes and lockouts","description":"","desc_html":"Days not worked, stoppages and workers involved in strikes and lockouts, from ILOSTAT.<br>Nothing like this exists in OECD's statistics. Strikes are the exercise of associational power rather than its stock, and the counts move on events rather than trends: a single national dispute can lift a country's figure by an order of magnitude for one year.<br>Use days not worked per thousand workers for comparison between countries; the raw counts mostly measure how large the workforce is.","desc_text":"Days not worked, stoppages and workers involved in strikes and lockouts, from ILOSTAT, for the whole economy.","topic":"UNION","dims":[{"id":"REF_AREA","name":"Country","ids":["ABW","AIA","ANT","ARG","ARM","ATG","AUS","AUT","BDI","BEL","BEN","BFA","BGD","BHR","BHS","BLR","BLZ","BMU","BOL","BRA","BRB","BTN","BWA","CAF","CAN","CHE","CHL","CMR","COL","CPV","CRI","CYM","CYP","CZE","DEU","DMA","DNK","DOM","DZA","ECU","EGY","ESP","EST","FIN","FJI","FRA","GAB","GBR","GEO","GHA","GIN","GRC","GTM","GUY","HKG","HND","HTI","HUN","IDN","IMN","IND","IRL","ISL","ISR","ITA","JAM","JOR","JPN","KEN","KHM","KOR","LKA","LTU","LVA","MAR","MDA","MDG","MEX","MLT","MMR","MNG","MUS","MYS","NAM","NCL","NER","NGA","NIC","NLD","NOR","NPL","NZL","PAK","PAN","PER","PHL","PNG","POL","PRI","PRT","PSE","ROU","RUS","RWA","SEN","SGP","SHN","SLV","SMR","SUR","SVK","SWE","SWZ","SYC","TGO","THA","TTO","TUN","TUR","UGA","UKR","URY","USA","VCT","VEN","ZAF","ZMB"],"names":["Aruba","Anguilla","ANT","Argentina","Armenia","Antigua and Barbuda","Australia","Austria","Burundi","Belgium","Benin","Burkina Faso","Bangladesh","Bahrain","Bahamas","Belarus","Belize","Bermuda","Bolivia","Brazil","Barbados","Bhutan","Botswana","Central African Republic","Canada","Switzerland","Chile","Cameroon","Colombia","Cabo Verde","Costa Rica","Cayman Islands","Cyprus","Czechia","Germany","Dominica","Denmark"